notes=UI scaled to 720p in the layout engine (menus match 480p; HUD keeps anchors; on-screen markers like the PK target circle follow their targets). Retail XBE (all section hashes verified). 1280x720 progressive using the game's own widescreen path. NTSC only. Enable 720p in the dashboard, component/HDMI out, REQUIRES 128MB RAM. Temporarily lifts the Cerbios 3.1.0 kernel's 64MB contiguous-memory limit while the game reserves its memory, then restores it (does nothing on other BIOSes). Skips Bink videos whose textures can't be created instead of crashing.
#XBE init flags 0x5->0x1: clear 'limit to 64MB' so a 128MB console gives the game the extra RAM 720p needs
0x00000124:01000000
#Kernel fix 1/3: header size 0xE38->0x1000 so the loader also maps the unused bytes after the header (used for the code below)
0x00000108:00100000
#Kernel fix 2/3 (code in header slack, VA 0x10E40): if this is Cerbios 3.1.0 (bytes DF3F0000 at 0x8002255F), raise MmAllocateContiguousMemoryEx's hard limit from page 0x3FDF (64MB) to 0x7FDF (128MB), then run the game's memory probe
0x00000E40:51B85F2502808138DF3F0000751A9CFA0F20C15181E1FFFFFEFF0F22C1C700DF7F0000590F22C19D59E942720C00
#Kernel fix 3/3: game memory probe now calls the kernel fix first (pool = largest block - 18MB, as originally, but the largest block can now be above 64MB)
0x000C8237:E8048CF3FF
#Memory limit: put Cerbios' 64MB contiguous limit back (7FDF -> 3FDF) right after the game reserves its pool, so soft reset (IGRDash), screenshots and later apps see a normal kernel (header slack VA 0x10F80)
0x00000F80:5051813D5E250280B9DF7F00751E9CFA0F20C15181E1FFFFFEFF0F22C1C7055F250280DF3F0000590F22C19D59588B159C0A2500E9A3720C00
